{"model": "Chatterbox Turbo (MLX 8-bit)", "segments": [{"text": "Summary", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8d83637eb79ecc1a98edcc2e8e2297c3bfa979dd04cf678a93b65efb74f40023.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.6]]}, {"text": "Design a web crawler that fetches every page on en.wikipedia.org exactly 1 time.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8048e4d2226d12337375067b97c3998412ad0311ab6f9d3f421b3f43d83f15f9.mp3"}, {"text": "You have 10,000 servers you can use and you are not allowed to fetch a URL more than once.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/461dd265cb332e43b1843d3ee31fd2f5c55220cbd0abb2cde665e38194d65fea.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.46], [3, 1.26, 1.7], [4, 1.7, 2.12], [5, 2.12, 2.26], [6, 2.26, 2.54], [7, 2.54, 2.82], [8, 2.82, 2.92], [9, 2.92, 3.0], [10, 3.0, 3.2], [11, 3.2, 3.48], [12, 3.48, 3.72], [13, 3.72, 3.94], [14, 3.94, 4.08], [15, 4.08, 4.38], [16, 4.38, 4.74], [17, 4.74, 4.9], [18, 4.9, 5.22]]}, {"text": "If a URL fails to be fetched (because of a timeout or server failure), it can be discarded.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/748397cca6da63fffaab99e867ee8e56555ab48fdde6458e3b598ab537941357.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.3], [2, 0.3, 0.66], [3, 0.66, 1.08], [4, 1.08, 1.34], [5, 1.34, 1.48], [6, 1.48, 1.98], [7, 1.98, 2.36], [8, 2.36, 2.54], [9, 2.54, 2.64], [10, 2.64, 3.02], [11, 3.02, 3.22], [12, 3.22, 3.52], [13, 3.52, 3.94], [14, 4.28, 4.48], [15, 4.48, 4.6], [16, 4.6, 4.74], [17, 4.74, 5.18]]}, {"text": "👉👉Have a question?", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/46eb735eb777b0c5e0d4bd901ea5d388223f605ab69cec1d67edf32cfa479b0d.mp3"}, {"text": "Join our FB group: System Designers", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/95bfbec574a5fa8015bc28445bc815ab79c82c8e73a23d6a8d3ffd7ebebd1c0c.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.3, 0.46], [2, 0.46, 0.82], [3, 0.82, 1.16], [5, 1.72, 2.28]]}, {"text": "Related Companies", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/e873822d46724173f69bd3788ea0c9f65e75fcf9e34e57c431bef08df5b6251a.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.4], [1, 0.4, 0.82]]}, {"text": "Facebook.com (Interview question)", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ea585556c8125a64c269d8bd97093b5068b36f11306e853dc2e7cd714df5f942.mp3"}, {"text": "Wikipedia.org (Example website to crawl)", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/4f2c3d86c7547595a11be8eab1921aefd35ab28005e2a54c301238c0e66c2873.mp3"}, {"text": "Archive.org", "block": 6, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/3f613ee64d5b7c53896917398c5b4668a14f661ff128f80bf99f4dbbe49f11a2.mp3"}, {"text": "Topics Discussed", "block": 7, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/750efd1e92b7a535d284e397f74aaccf8e95a866d648f56ad7dce9b8d0a6864e.mp3"}, {"text": "Hashing", "block": 8, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/1f2f6a368fab977524354fa7f39016a2ec31d26a0bb4dc011eb0f566bec9aea3.mp3"}, {"text": "Distributed Systems", "block": 9, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/a57e2c21ccacac875e0c795bec2c96c50a13d887fe6e65b777ae2c0efd9cc576.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.48], [1, 0.48, 0.96]]}, {"text": "Consistent Hashing", "block": 10, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/3df37106471bfb56d2df4617f9c13619e5bfc8c85d786703d0d1ea8326d889a5.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.54], [1, 0.54, 1.08]]}, {"text": "Bloom Filter", "block": 11, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/da58adfafd8e1910945f47107d90dc3ff1899c150c6ae3f50a0f60f2bf9adcdd.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.3], [1, 0.3, 0.74]]}, {"text": "Trie Data Structures", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/431a778b4ea259b682e2e49282e63210ab3af2124ac0f32b2fc0b61b13ef48b3.mp3"}, {"text": "Consumer Groups (Kafka)", "block": 13, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/731ddce3796b2932570574115fa46ed85eaebcacb42f217a638dcca1e9aa9329.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.44], [1, 0.44, 0.98]]}, {"text": "Paxos", "block": 14, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/35e07abcb78e192939ded9364968c8e3ad6a38a461ec26403a868c167e5d50c4.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.72]]}, {"text": "Requirements", "block": 15, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/0615a539c2fc680c8ffc118cee430aba5e4f01664f34f1b629da6ad9f18ce5aa.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.82]]}, {"text": "Functional", "block": 16, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b513383e6843d6372f6d96e4ad19d35427e28cc94bd06c70efb246313480460f.mp3"}, {"text": "Download all (6.5m) URLs from en.wikipedia.com", "block": 17, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ee001715bc3bcb215acb237b0ca483859d50f51a301a20872130dd03da364fd4.mp3"}, {"text": "Only download each URL once", "block": 18, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/33e26bbb969a7e197b7fe592dcbc94f096366f693bf7ea48a50e922d50e2cedb.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.3], [1, 0.3, 0.72], [2, 0.72, 1.06], [3, 1.06, 1.36], [4, 1.36, 1.88]]}, {"text": "Using 10k 2-core servers", "block": 19, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ce7992721afaa09b5f2d421c2dff8c9f1cca73dbcb280ad3a383d1a05ec84638.mp3"}, {"text": "Only processing on the content is extract URLs otherwise persist the content to local storage", "block": 20, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b6c48821d2ba12390213eb80394f8cd164b7325b51fe2cdeeafe116236270ba1.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.26], [1, 0.26, 0.74], [2, 0.74, 0.94], [3, 0.94, 1.04], [4, 1.04, 1.42], [5, 1.42, 1.74], [6, 1.74, 2.1], [7, 2.1, 2.54], [8, 2.88, 3.18], [9, 3.18, 3.64], [10, 3.64, 3.88], [11, 3.88, 4.24], [12, 4.24, 4.46], [13, 4.46, 4.66], [14, 4.66, 5.08]]}, {"text": "Don’t crawl images", "block": 21, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/bcf24803487b437ee7f8d9c9b3f3943fd799a1d7bd166e7cef95b5fe81531bde.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.32], [1, 0.32, 0.46], [2, 0.46, 0.88]]}, {"text": "Only crawl English Wikipedia", "block": 22, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/956d3a89b74402318f4853851bdb19daf31f4eaca63cc6fa2b96d2cb73afd2e4.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.4], [2, 0.74, 1.22], [3, 1.22, 1.8]]}, {"text": "Minimize network traffic between each server.", "block": 23, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8205a3b4aed648a969ea59e8a6f561bd5e966ebd6d70c755fa66fc6f144c9eaf.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.52], [1, 0.52, 0.88], [2, 0.88, 1.34], [3, 1.34, 1.72], [4, 1.72, 2.04], [5, 2.04, 2.34]]}, {"text": "Non-functional", "block": 24, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/5b9beb402db39af7d766324e9d8e76d63deaceab646361dde601603f776e65e6.mp3"}, {"text": "No need to self-rate limit", "block": 25, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/997517fa5a0180202c53c8948f9a327fd6befb13043fccd3d5344c1bed2b4314.mp3"}, {"text": "Fetch the content as fast as possible", "block": 26, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/759779023b7652d2ab3696a263833fb1f0ac7590daef18c191e0d613731d4d02.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.42], [2, 0.42, 0.84], [3, 0.84, 1.24], [4, 1.24, 1.52], [5, 1.52, 1.72], [6, 1.72, 2.2]]}, {"text": "High-level Analysis", "block": 27, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/396a2480511a69707a8ee325e269d8ebb535854eca6d8a7048ca2f2b594a2b1e.mp3"}, {"text": "How much storage will we need to store 6,500,000 URLs and their HTML documents?", "block": 28, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8e8fc1015cf2218073db1a11b99391933d9d2dbc5600aa836145bec0a462af66.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.44], [2, 0.44, 0.78], [3, 0.78, 1.02], [4, 1.02, 1.14], [5, 1.14, 1.28], [6, 1.28, 1.44], [7, 1.44, 1.66], [9, 3.36, 3.74], [10, 3.74, 4.1], [11, 4.1, 4.24], [12, 4.24, 4.68], [13, 4.68, 5.32]]}, {"text": "The average internet URL length is 66 characters.", "block": 29, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/fc3ca1f63134bbd239d8b260641ee480a6edeea9829c8b41b715a59cde5395dd.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.54], [2, 0.54, 0.94], [3, 0.94, 1.34], [4, 1.34, 1.78], [5, 1.78, 2.0], [6, 2.0, 2.36], [7, 2.36, 2.94]]}, {"text": "Since we don’t need to track the domain name or HTTPS prefix, we will round down to 60 characters.", "block": 29, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/6d91b29d5ce25e739ad4efddab531920fbebf89bb2900e6fbc716cb5bdabcc66.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.56], [3, 0.56, 0.66], [4, 0.66, 0.78], [5, 0.78, 0.98], [6, 0.98, 1.18], [7, 1.18, 1.42], [8, 1.42, 1.68], [9, 1.68, 1.88], [11, 2.62, 3.02], [12, 3.28, 3.32], [13, 3.32, 3.44], [14, 3.44, 3.66], [15, 3.66, 3.92], [16, 3.92, 4.1], [17, 4.1, 4.44], [18, 4.44, 4.92]]}, {"text": "The average HTML page is about 100kb.", "block": 30, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/dba2adb103591ac0bf12bccca96e385c48dbe746c3949d5d3a15e5c02db3e69c.mp3"}, {"text": "How do we want to store the URLs?", "block": 31, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/652d94da507541890529842f8d7ed63e958de832257e14af4e593cb50d93e4a2.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.32], [2, 0.32, 0.42], [3, 0.42, 0.56], [4, 0.56, 0.64], [5, 0.64, 0.86], [6, 0.86, 1.02], [7, 1.02, 1.4]]}, {"text": "Similar to the URL shortening system design problems, the most practical way of storing URLs that we have visited is a Set Structure for O(1) lookup.", "block": 32, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d80b8ea7c51ddd444973e2ae0b14b4e89df584c821249c87233e81bbbebfdd52.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.34], [1, 0.34, 0.58], [2, 0.58, 0.72], [3, 0.72, 1.0], [4, 1.0, 1.54], [5, 1.54, 1.92], [6, 1.92, 2.24], [7, 2.24, 2.74], [8, 3.06, 3.14], [9, 3.14, 3.38], [10, 3.38, 3.82], [11, 3.82, 4.08], [12, 4.08, 4.22], [13, 4.22, 4.5], [14, 4.5, 4.94], [15, 4.94, 5.2], [16, 5.2, 5.34], [17, 5.34, 5.46], [18, 5.46, 5.84], [19, 5.84, 6.1], [20, 6.1, 6.2], [21, 6.2, 6.38], [22, 6.38, 6.82], [23, 6.82, 7.1], [25, 7.52, 8.42]]}, {"text": "While the hashes approach will consume more memory, since we will be storing the full URL, than a Trie Data Structure or binary search tree, the lookups will be much faster (O(1) vs O(n)) and the additional memory cost will be manageable.", "block": 32, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/162a338a9d50f2b8d1a0a44da64b6c61d003df345b679ec37c60ca54825cd233.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.26], [1, 0.26, 0.46], [3, 0.84, 1.12], [4, 1.12, 1.32], [5, 1.32, 1.66], [6, 1.66, 1.96], [7, 1.96, 2.3], [8, 2.3, 2.7], [9, 2.7, 2.92], [10, 2.92, 3.02], [11, 3.02, 3.16], [12, 3.16, 3.4], [13, 3.4, 3.6], [14, 3.6, 3.82], [15, 3.82, 4.1], [16, 4.1, 4.66], [17, 4.66, 4.84], [19, 5.06, 5.34], [20, 5.34, 5.78], [21, 5.78, 6.04], [22, 6.04, 6.38], [23, 6.38, 6.74], [24, 6.74, 7.12], [25, 7.56, 7.78], [26, 7.78, 8.1], [27, 8.1, 8.24], [28, 8.24, 8.36], [29, 8.36, 8.56], [30, 8.56, 9.06], [34, 12.5, 12.7], [35, 12.7, 12.82], [36, 12.82, 13.2], [37, 13.2, 13.52], [38, 13.52, 13.86], [39, 13.86, 14.12], [40, 14.12, 14.24], [41, 14.24, 14.68]]}, {"text": "Where can we store the URLs?", "block": 33, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/aba4d0fc5fd904d78e9d68daa4b8fde7e8c098674694a2e177146dd481be5ffc.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.48], [2, 0.48, 0.58], [3, 0.58, 0.88], [4, 0.88, 1.06], [5, 1.06, 1.42]]}, {"text": "390 Megabytes for all URLs can easily be stored in RAM, meaning we can get away with using an in-memory RAM solution for managing which URLs we have tracked.", "block": 34, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/795b6f445a68157f3c38293b638350c95b13942dabd75e02f015ed7be29eb639.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.64, 1.18], [2, 1.18, 1.42], [3, 1.42, 1.62], [4, 1.62, 1.96], [5, 1.96, 2.36], [6, 2.36, 2.72], [7, 2.72, 2.94], [8, 2.94, 3.24], [9, 3.24, 3.46], [10, 3.46, 3.66], [11, 4.1, 4.36], [12, 4.36, 4.58], [13, 4.58, 4.72], [14, 4.72, 4.86], [15, 4.86, 5.08], [16, 5.08, 5.28], [17, 5.28, 5.6], [18, 5.6, 5.8], [20, 6.28, 6.52], [21, 6.52, 7.02], [22, 7.02, 7.3], [23, 7.3, 7.64], [24, 7.64, 7.94], [25, 7.94, 8.38], [26, 8.38, 8.72], [27, 8.72, 8.82], [28, 8.82, 9.12]]}, {"text": "65 Gigabytes is more than we can cost-effectively store in RAM on a single server.", "block": 35, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/6b7d2111feace2de76d8b6c15b170d93a7eba34b8a4415a36d0d726d03e8b818.mp3"}, {"text": "If we need to store the documents on a single server, we will need to write to the local hard drive.", "block": 35, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/1c3aae3d557926140879041d0b49cde32a1de39cc254f0a956e6f91bca610e6b.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.54], [3, 0.54, 0.72], [4, 0.72, 0.92], [5, 0.92, 1.06], [6, 1.06, 1.5], [7, 1.5, 1.8], [8, 1.8, 1.9], [9, 1.9, 2.18], [10, 2.18, 2.62], [11, 3.16, 3.34], [12, 3.34, 3.46], [13, 3.46, 3.6], [14, 3.6, 3.78], [15, 3.78, 3.9], [16, 3.9, 4.1], [17, 4.1, 4.2], [18, 4.2, 4.44], [19, 4.44, 4.72], [20, 4.72, 5.0]]}, {"text": "Because we have 10,000 servers, we could evenly distribute the documents, so each server would only need to store 3.9 GB of HTML.", "block": 35, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/1873856df611be2b929ad88b0f165ec06a583df23d5c3f948e1f0ba5573260eb.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.5], [2, 0.5, 0.6], [4, 1.24, 1.62], [5, 1.88, 1.96], [6, 1.96, 2.1], [7, 2.1, 2.48], [8, 2.48, 2.88], [9, 2.88, 3.12], [10, 3.12, 3.54], [11, 4.04, 4.2], [12, 4.2, 4.44], [13, 4.44, 4.78], [14, 4.78, 4.98], [15, 4.98, 5.24], [16, 5.24, 5.46], [17, 5.46, 5.62], [18, 5.62, 5.86], [21, 7.14, 7.58], [22, 7.58, 8.0]]}, {"text": "3.9 GB can easily be stored in RAM at a reasonable price.", "block": 35, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/2455d9e82b6a2b36d4731b684f5826f019a5928fabdd8385614d0052ea547ad8.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.64, 0.98], [2, 0.98, 1.26], [3, 1.26, 1.62], [4, 1.62, 1.8], [5, 1.8, 2.04], [6, 2.04, 2.24], [7, 2.24, 2.5], [8, 2.5, 2.78], [9, 2.78, 2.88], [10, 2.88, 3.12], [11, 3.12, 3.54]]}, {"text": "Where will be the limitations?", "block": 36, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8cbf234f7c36eed42d50270c5cca99ca49f6bea0dfd2ecfbb3a88cf2ba5b887b.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.48], [3, 0.48, 0.56], [4, 0.56, 1.0]]}, {"text": "CPU?", "block": 36, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/6ddeea047a2ac6c45d426c6e47c80e3ce63fc0202aab46936f05ea7292ee2770.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.38]]}, {"text": "Disk?", "block": 36, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/914605c0e41c49ebb4a4af5dbb66a95290a6865607d995b268a9f18eff6e1373.mp3"}, {"text": "Network?", "block": 36, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8d070ade452c37fa50b8cacbb9b5a11ed31eea89e794f24f5eb08db4f8f93b3d.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.36]]}, {"text": "CPU: The most expensive task for the CPU will be extracting the URLs to be crawled from the HTML documents crawled so far.", "block": 37, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/bb731037bd63e741e1baa17e024cbca3800b8d7af43e2c725efd802b88a07f27.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.42], [1, 0.84, 0.94], [2, 0.94, 1.14], [3, 1.14, 1.62], [5, 1.96, 2.26], [6, 2.26, 2.38], [7, 2.38, 2.78], [8, 2.78, 3.1], [9, 3.1, 3.26], [10, 3.26, 3.74], [11, 3.74, 4.0], [12, 4.0, 4.4], [13, 4.4, 4.76], [14, 4.76, 4.86], [15, 4.86, 5.24], [16, 5.24, 5.4], [17, 5.4, 5.58], [18, 5.58, 6.04], [19, 6.04, 6.7], [20, 6.7, 7.08], [21, 7.08, 7.26], [22, 7.26, 7.56]]}, {"text": "This task should take less than 1ms per document.", "block": 37, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/78291027ca8e4e7f9a0cb7fd109df7cb16478fbbada0d7c96db1cbaf83a9fdd7.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.26], [1, 0.26, 0.58], [2, 0.58, 0.82], [3, 0.82, 0.98], [4, 0.98, 1.26], [5, 1.26, 1.58], [6, 1.58, 2.24], [7, 2.24, 2.56], [8, 2.56, 2.98]]}, {"text": "Disk: As mentioned above, we probably don’t need to be writing to disk at all since the documents, when distributed across the 10k servers, will fit into memory.", "block": 38, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/472f45d8530c077f992465ae82d8f9fde1f359f578a6d7c2b40ee92e05de23da.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.74, 0.82], [2, 0.82, 1.16], [3, 1.16, 1.46], [4, 1.76, 1.84], [5, 1.84, 2.2], [6, 2.2, 2.62], [7, 2.62, 2.86], [8, 2.86, 3.1], [9, 3.1, 3.22], [10, 3.22, 3.48], [11, 3.48, 3.72], [13, 4.02, 4.18], [14, 4.18, 4.4], [15, 4.4, 4.66], [16, 4.66, 4.84], [17, 4.84, 5.32], [18, 5.74, 5.9], [19, 5.9, 6.4], [20, 6.4, 6.76], [21, 6.76, 7.06], [22, 7.06, 7.42], [23, 7.42, 7.82], [24, 7.82, 8.4], [25, 8.4, 8.64], [26, 8.64, 8.92], [27, 8.92, 9.22]]}, {"text": "Network: Round trip to wikipedia.org for a single document may take ~200ms depending on their load and the distance our servers will be from theirs.", "block": 39, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/7491b7a3fcfaaf6780cb62bc7fee2558f488955788892feff6674671cf113545.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.36], [5, 2.16, 2.38], [6, 2.38, 2.5], [7, 2.5, 2.74], [8, 2.74, 3.28], [9, 3.28, 3.5], [10, 3.5, 3.82], [12, 4.66, 5.06], [13, 5.06, 5.34], [14, 5.34, 5.48], [15, 5.48, 5.8], [16, 5.8, 6.22], [17, 6.22, 6.3], [18, 6.3, 6.58], [19, 6.58, 6.8], [20, 6.8, 7.16], [21, 7.16, 7.32], [22, 7.32, 7.48], [23, 7.48, 7.68], [24, 7.68, 7.96]]}, {"text": "This will be a Network bound task with the opportunity while waiting for the network responses for our CPUs to parse the existing HTML documents of their URLs.", "block": 40, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8d4513897b52d3d59e83aad1ee13d0452ae47f1ae34cf21a7b4dd5a180d54e4a.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.26], [1, 0.26, 0.4], [2, 0.4, 0.56], [3, 0.56, 0.68], [4, 0.68, 0.98], [6, 1.28, 1.64], [7, 1.64, 1.96], [8, 1.96, 2.06], [9, 2.06, 2.62], [10, 2.62, 3.2], [11, 3.2, 3.5], [12, 3.5, 3.72], [13, 3.72, 3.84], [14, 3.84, 4.12], [15, 4.12, 4.76], [16, 4.76, 5.02], [17, 5.02, 5.16], [18, 5.16, 5.82], [19, 5.82, 5.94], [20, 5.94, 6.2], [21, 6.2, 6.42], [22, 6.42, 6.82], [23, 6.82, 7.36], [24, 7.36, 7.88], [25, 7.88, 8.16], [26, 8.16, 8.3], [27, 8.3, 8.7]]}, {"text": "Design Options", "block": 41, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/1b062215d4d98988e7db55266495c1ee533f213c153cb03f6f4d26a6059fda12.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.4], [1, 0.4, 0.84]]}, {"text": "Option 1: Single server", "block": 42, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/e616a3e62fea28128471dd3e5a4752ab698d15fb3175bb21987be3b04809e1f0.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.36], [1, 0.36, 0.86], [2, 1.16, 1.42], [3, 1.42, 1.82]]}, {"text": "We will start simple and expand to maximize the resources of the problem.", "block": 43, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/13a94194b3b95a849899d13fd4836c7339f981d13524894c1bc0981c6637797c.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.32], [2, 0.32, 0.54], [3, 0.54, 0.92], [4, 0.92, 1.24], [5, 1.24, 1.54], [6, 1.54, 1.88], [7, 1.88, 2.28], [8, 2.28, 2.58], [9, 2.58, 2.96], [10, 2.96, 3.22], [11, 3.22, 3.32], [12, 3.32, 3.66]]}, {"text": "A naive approach would be for a single server to fetch a URL, extract the URLs from the document and then query the next URL", "block": 44, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8aa1877794250ffca58cd64f749b399a489507b366d263f3caefb891dbdbbbb9.mp3", "words": [[2, 0.44, 0.98], [3, 0.98, 1.34], [4, 1.34, 1.5], [5, 1.5, 1.66], [6, 1.66, 1.78], [7, 1.78, 2.06], [8, 2.06, 2.5], [9, 2.5, 2.74], [10, 2.74, 2.96], [11, 2.96, 3.12], [12, 3.12, 3.48], [13, 4.02, 4.38], [14, 4.38, 4.7], [15, 4.7, 5.02], [16, 5.02, 5.46], [17, 5.46, 5.6], [18, 5.6, 6.04], [19, 6.38, 6.62], [20, 6.62, 6.78], [21, 6.78, 7.12], [22, 7.12, 7.34], [23, 7.34, 7.6], [24, 7.6, 7.96]]}, {"text": "Follow up questions they may ask:", "block": 45, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/af81b651ae8541f26c57db7eb00c9b3d23283efe3181057f7d9823377d28f5d9.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.3], [1, 0.3, 0.54], [2, 0.54, 0.94], [3, 0.94, 1.28], [4, 1.28, 1.42], [5, 1.42, 1.76]]}, {"text": "How do we know how many URLs we can safely fetch from one server at a time?", "block": 46, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/eec4836e47622472ad2361d6b506356ada866b922ccf15eab96b04e3d8f2c3bb.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.32], [2, 0.32, 0.44], [3, 0.44, 0.66], [4, 0.66, 0.94], [5, 0.94, 1.1], [6, 1.1, 1.54], [7, 1.54, 1.88], [8, 1.88, 2.02], [9, 2.02, 2.26], [10, 2.26, 2.62], [11, 2.62, 2.84], [12, 2.84, 3.02], [13, 3.02, 3.28], [14, 3.28, 3.48], [15, 3.48, 3.56], [16, 3.56, 3.84]]}, {"text": "For this, we will need to experiment with timeouts to determine when we are rate limited.", "block": 47, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/4f877579fa0d26ab3396bb064f71f4f459e9bbd68a9d0ff2649b7c1870d0e08d.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.46], [2, 0.82, 1.02], [3, 1.02, 1.12], [4, 1.12, 1.28], [5, 1.28, 1.46], [6, 1.46, 1.92], [7, 1.92, 2.3], [9, 2.8, 2.98], [10, 2.98, 3.36], [11, 3.36, 3.66], [12, 3.66, 3.86], [13, 3.86, 3.98], [14, 3.98, 4.16], [15, 4.16, 4.52]]}, {"text": "Typically systems throttle too many connections coming from a single ip address to prevent them from abusing the service.", "block": 47, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d5b302c15b1e250a53e9c36f5208a1641c18b64c04f3805254dd786390386dc9.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.44], [1, 0.44, 0.92], [2, 0.92, 1.28], [3, 1.28, 1.54], [4, 1.54, 1.76], [5, 1.76, 2.2], [6, 2.2, 2.62], [7, 2.62, 2.82], [8, 2.82, 2.96], [9, 2.96, 3.24], [12, 3.76, 4.12], [13, 4.12, 4.4], [14, 4.4, 4.64], [15, 4.64, 4.82], [16, 4.82, 5.18], [17, 5.18, 5.38], [18, 5.38, 5.7]]}, {"text": "Pros", "block": 48, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b629726cd0b7234801e4206158e2f3f01af19022d4ec31a955fc5ec72c680845.mp3"}, {"text": "Simple", "block": 49, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/3dea45ccea131f62eefa76b2ab967a249fd45652ba8e2f14dd9a13163f16a04a.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.38]]}, {"text": "Cons", "block": 50, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/888f900af800cdcbd6e947bed17fded4d9661d7ebf0cfc0bf47316d9b8bec67b.mp3"}, {"text": "Does not utilize the 10k servers", "block": 51, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/5ec46574e1b2f887345ce4c425262a2535d3f69f4c1e4b299bea2ead727b18c3.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.2, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.8], [3, 0.8, 1.06], [4, 1.06, 1.38], [5, 1.38, 1.74]]}, {"text": "Wastes CPU cycles waiting for the web request to complete", "block": 52, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8612ff7fd28af4b53c27b83fb93200d0f6205cb08fbc087e753a9ba187849913.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.38, 0.78], [2, 0.78, 1.2], [3, 1.2, 1.54], [4, 1.54, 1.76], [5, 1.76, 1.88], [6, 1.88, 2.04], [7, 2.04, 2.4], [8, 2.4, 2.6], [9, 2.6, 2.92]]}, {"text": "A server failure results in complete data loss", "block": 53, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/43e189fefd474ed04d55e387559d24bbafffb3889ad8486010f33e3389aa610c.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.48], [2, 0.48, 0.9], [4, 1.22, 1.48], [5, 1.48, 1.86], [6, 1.86, 2.2], [7, 2.2, 2.52]]}, {"text": "👉👉Have a question?", "block": 54, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/46eb735eb777b0c5e0d4bd901ea5d388223f605ab69cec1d67edf32cfa479b0d.mp3"}, {"text": "Join our FB group: System Designers", "block": 54, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/95bfbec574a5fa8015bc28445bc815ab79c82c8e73a23d6a8d3ffd7ebebd1c0c.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.3, 0.46], [2, 0.46, 0.82], [3, 0.82, 1.16], [5, 1.72, 2.28]]}, {"text": "Option 2: Distributed Systems", "block": 55, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/a4437afee1f59b696f83544c6c0e727eb2e80d01e7c08c24d6b07110a80ef26b.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.36], [1, 0.36, 0.82], [2, 1.1, 1.56], [3, 1.56, 2.0]]}, {"text": "Assigning each URL to a specific server lets each server manage which URLs need to be fetched or have already been fetched.", "block": 56, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/1158428b80752701f61c4f435d3ac39f26652b4bfac2905018780b5b6672f10d.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.5], [1, 0.5, 0.86], [2, 0.86, 1.24], [3, 1.24, 1.58], [4, 1.58, 1.66], [5, 1.66, 2.02], [6, 2.02, 2.42], [7, 2.42, 2.72], [8, 2.72, 3.08], [9, 3.08, 3.36], [10, 3.36, 3.74], [11, 3.74, 4.02], [12, 4.02, 4.54], [13, 4.54, 4.9], [14, 4.9, 5.06], [15, 5.06, 5.18], [16, 5.18, 5.68], [17, 5.68, 5.96], [18, 5.96, 6.14], [19, 6.14, 6.34], [20, 6.34, 6.54], [21, 6.54, 7.06]]}, {"text": "Each server will get its own id number starting from 0 to 99,999.", "block": 56, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/7c1e67ec6c77bde046071eedad981d251f798d9d7e2c6b9a47cbff68f3843db6.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.62], [2, 0.62, 0.82], [3, 0.82, 0.98], [4, 0.98, 1.18], [5, 1.18, 1.38], [6, 1.38, 1.56], [7, 1.56, 1.84], [8, 1.84, 2.18], [9, 2.18, 2.42], [10, 2.42, 2.74], [11, 2.74, 3.0]]}, {"text": "Hashing each URL and calculating the modulus of the hash with 10,000 can define the id of the server we need to fetch the URL from.", "block": 56, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/80a360e6b5a04cdb02cd46331542321fafda725b45a18c1ddf582dbde40ed1b8.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.42], [3, 1.34, 1.56], [4, 1.56, 2.02], [5, 2.02, 2.3], [6, 2.3, 2.62], [7, 2.62, 2.88], [8, 2.88, 3.02], [9, 3.02, 3.2], [10, 3.2, 3.42], [12, 4.02, 4.24], [13, 4.24, 4.58], [14, 4.58, 4.84], [16, 5.02, 5.3], [17, 5.3, 5.44], [18, 5.44, 5.8], [19, 5.8, 6.04], [20, 6.04, 6.18], [21, 6.18, 6.32], [22, 6.32, 6.58], [23, 6.58, 6.74], [24, 6.74, 7.06], [25, 7.06, 7.4]]}, {"text": "In a master/slave design, a single master server could map the server ids to specific ip addresses.", "block": 57, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8e09a1ba81c688bdb159db3414b6adc2182a3802cdab7b0dc0cb05158ad350b8.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.28], [3, 0.96, 1.38], [4, 1.74, 1.8], [5, 1.8, 2.1], [6, 2.1, 2.46], [7, 2.46, 2.84], [8, 2.84, 3.08], [9, 3.08, 3.28], [10, 3.28, 3.5], [11, 3.5, 3.76], [14, 3.98, 4.54], [16, 4.86, 5.22]]}, {"text": "Since the problem asks us to reduce network traffic, we can either pre-configure each server with an id to ip address or rely on a DNS server to map hostnames to ip addresses (e.g. 123.crawler.company.com points to server 123).", "block": 57, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/68490fff4a79d0b061242edfc9544e7bc0669c9c0741c370aa9a0f285b182cc3.mp3"}, {"text": "In case there is a failure and the server id needs to be assigned to a new server, the dns record would be updated to point to the new healthy server.", "block": 57, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b6568c94ef193b5f75f8b5698971070639c024084c576e00131a353c456efb3d.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.4], [4, 0.78, 0.84], [5, 0.84, 1.18], [6, 1.18, 1.48], [7, 1.48, 1.62], [8, 1.62, 1.92], [10, 2.14, 2.38], [11, 2.38, 2.62], [12, 2.62, 2.74], [13, 2.74, 2.96], [14, 2.96, 3.22], [15, 3.22, 3.28], [16, 3.28, 3.4], [17, 3.4, 3.76], [18, 4.18, 4.3], [19, 4.3, 4.54], [20, 4.54, 4.98], [21, 4.98, 5.2], [22, 5.2, 5.32], [23, 5.32, 5.72], [24, 5.72, 5.96], [25, 5.96, 6.16], [26, 6.16, 6.38], [27, 6.38, 6.46], [28, 6.46, 6.68], [30, 7.04, 7.44]]}, {"text": "Since every URL will be uniquely assigned to a single server number, each server will internally track which URLs it has already crawled, just like the single server design.", "block": 58, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b7b31e58b43f7d1b6a41d0761c08c2182ccd25ad59f3fd3987ce36f11fa5ceff.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.34], [1, 0.34, 0.64], [2, 0.64, 0.98], [3, 0.98, 1.32], [4, 1.32, 1.46], [5, 1.46, 1.86], [6, 1.86, 2.24], [7, 2.24, 2.5], [8, 2.5, 2.58], [9, 2.58, 2.8], [10, 2.8, 3.12], [11, 3.12, 3.48], [12, 3.92, 4.06], [13, 4.06, 4.48], [14, 4.48, 4.7], [15, 4.7, 5.16], [16, 5.16, 5.5], [17, 5.5, 5.76], [18, 5.76, 6.2], [19, 6.2, 6.58], [20, 6.58, 6.7], [21, 6.7, 6.96], [22, 6.96, 7.46], [23, 7.62, 7.88], [24, 7.88, 8.04], [25, 8.04, 8.2], [26, 8.2, 8.42], [27, 8.42, 8.76], [28, 8.76, 9.06]]}, {"text": "The single server design uses a set, but we could also use a Bloom Filter.", "block": 58, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/0c94718b2d23f3b9e540cf9768b98215810a8379f807e1199189cfcb44821b3a.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.42], [2, 0.42, 0.78], [3, 0.78, 1.08], [4, 1.08, 1.42], [5, 1.42, 1.6], [6, 1.6, 1.8], [7, 1.98, 2.08], [8, 2.08, 2.22], [9, 2.22, 2.34], [10, 2.34, 2.52], [11, 2.52, 2.76], [12, 2.76, 2.88], [13, 2.88, 3.06], [14, 3.06, 3.44]]}, {"text": "APIs", "block": 59, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/95f38ef2192293737bae14e75d539b87e3c764b3e235a1ee12eb93afdc1b4547.mp3"}, {"text": "Each server will need to implement an API to receive a set of URLs that the other servers find in their pages.", "block": 60, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/c15202a98e63fb50fe827811ac7c3385dd64eef5a722868c8830d8e69dc620ab.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.36], [1, 0.36, 0.66], [2, 0.66, 0.86], [3, 0.86, 1.06], [4, 1.06, 1.22], [5, 1.22, 1.54], [6, 1.54, 1.78], [7, 1.78, 2.2], [8, 2.2, 2.56], [9, 2.56, 2.84], [10, 2.84, 3.04], [11, 3.04, 3.24], [12, 3.24, 3.38], [13, 3.38, 3.74], [14, 3.74, 4.18], [15, 4.18, 4.34], [16, 4.34, 4.5], [17, 4.5, 4.92], [18, 4.92, 5.32], [19, 5.32, 5.54], [20, 5.54, 5.64], [21, 5.64, 6.02]]}, {"text": "We can use JSON and REST to route these requests.", "block": 60, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/dfdd29b1afbb298df5df8c1ae8ba72b35b25f2043e19c876ab9170760a858ba7.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.58], [3, 0.58, 1.0], [4, 1.0, 1.24], [5, 1.24, 1.54], [6, 1.54, 1.7], [7, 1.7, 1.92], [8, 1.92, 2.14], [9, 2.14, 2.5]]}, {"text": "The URLs attribute should be a unique list of URLs found in the html documents that the server found at its own URLs.", "block": 61, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/1cd42af7c363a66f4a763b3964914f3c71441ab975532cb7fede97330c9d6ffb.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.94], [2, 0.94, 1.4], [3, 1.4, 1.68], [4, 1.68, 1.84], [5, 1.84, 1.98], [6, 1.98, 2.32], [7, 2.32, 2.84], [8, 2.84, 3.08], [9, 3.08, 3.46], [10, 3.46, 3.96], [11, 3.96, 4.18], [12, 4.18, 4.28], [13, 4.28, 4.64], [14, 4.64, 5.38], [15, 5.38, 5.68], [16, 5.68, 5.82], [17, 5.82, 6.1], [18, 6.1, 6.56], [19, 6.56, 6.76], [20, 6.76, 6.96], [21, 6.96, 7.26], [22, 7.26, 7.66]]}, {"text": "We should avoid sending 1 web request per document because each network request has overhead.", "block": 61, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/46a740c2cc88d4b0c6148d948075991a5096237ee05b7cfbcb8043036e2e3e7b.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.12], [1, 0.12, 0.26], [2, 0.26, 0.52], [3, 0.52, 0.92], [5, 1.22, 1.52], [6, 1.52, 1.8], [7, 1.8, 2.06], [8, 2.06, 2.5], [9, 2.5, 2.8], [10, 2.8, 3.08], [11, 3.08, 3.36], [12, 3.36, 3.8], [13, 3.8, 4.08], [14, 4.08, 4.52]]}, {"text": "We could collect URLs and send them to the other machines in batches of 100.", "block": 61, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ba1813b672438ebc9bbe88c0c6030d387d72dc4d1e1835d1029229ef0b5452ba.mp3", "words": [[3, 0.56, 1.02], [4, 1.02, 1.46], [5, 1.46, 1.66], [6, 1.66, 1.88], [7, 1.88, 2.02], [8, 2.02, 2.14], [9, 2.14, 2.32], [10, 2.32, 2.7], [11, 2.7, 3.04], [12, 3.04, 3.52], [13, 3.52, 3.7], [14, 3.7, 4.16]]}, {"text": "If we sent the URLs to the other machines as we extract them, each document may trigger N-network requests for each URL.", "block": 61, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/773c561d95ed13f18c787c34932379166577eddfa0001108dc22c9f4feda5f47.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.34], [3, 0.52, 0.68], [4, 0.68, 0.88], [5, 0.88, 1.32], [6, 1.32, 1.44], [7, 1.44, 1.62], [8, 1.62, 1.98], [9, 1.98, 2.2], [10, 2.2, 2.32], [11, 2.32, 2.66], [12, 2.66, 3.14], [13, 3.66, 3.82], [14, 3.82, 4.24], [15, 4.24, 4.5], [16, 4.5, 4.82], [18, 5.34, 5.78], [19, 5.78, 6.1], [20, 6.1, 6.36], [21, 6.36, 6.72]]}, {"text": "[Source]", "block": 62, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/62f7ec14de8ab9b7106637d89d7b2871cdd953f0cde2a4c762053b5326005395.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.58]]}, {"text": "Follow up questions:", "block": 63, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/28bd3e284849807106983286f3e3e89b76599772bc3e1928afb30d1a16af8aee.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.36], [1, 0.36, 0.54], [2, 0.54, 1.06]]}, {"text": "How can you distribute the URLs if a portion of the 10k servers lose power while the crawl is happening?", "block": 64, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/db4f08345e1b2b1450d45a751e4ee7105a8e8fd388a7124bdb580fc7d8119ec2.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.4], [2, 0.4, 0.5], [3, 0.5, 0.96], [4, 0.96, 1.18], [5, 1.18, 1.56], [6, 1.56, 1.92], [7, 1.92, 2.0], [8, 2.0, 2.3], [9, 2.3, 2.46], [10, 2.46, 2.58], [11, 2.58, 2.92], [12, 2.92, 3.26], [13, 3.26, 3.56], [14, 3.56, 4.0], [15, 4.0, 4.24], [16, 4.24, 4.38], [17, 4.38, 4.56], [18, 4.56, 4.74], [19, 4.74, 5.06]]}, {"text": "Borrowing from Kafka’s system design, we can use the concept of “consumer groups”.", "block": 65, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/babacbadc56e2936acfcc605dc1dc9cf626859963df74b0017c3e0450a9c46a8.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.42, 0.6], [4, 1.3, 1.74], [5, 2.06, 2.2], [6, 2.2, 2.34], [7, 2.34, 2.52], [8, 2.52, 2.64], [9, 2.64, 2.96], [10, 2.96, 3.2], [11, 3.2, 3.64], [12, 3.64, 4.02]]}, {"text": "Instead of sending the URLs to be fetched to a single machine, we could divide the 10,000 servers into groups that are collectively responsible for managing the URLs assigned to their group.", "block": 65, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/e17914cebd09b95c584c28d15848edfa104bac1cb11cd25170e2d08c199e09d8.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.4], [1, 0.4, 0.54], [2, 0.54, 0.78], [3, 0.78, 1.04], [4, 1.04, 1.34], [5, 1.34, 1.76], [6, 1.76, 1.9], [7, 1.9, 2.38], [8, 2.38, 2.54], [9, 2.54, 2.62], [10, 2.62, 2.9], [11, 2.9, 3.26], [12, 3.86, 3.94], [13, 3.94, 4.06], [14, 4.06, 4.38], [15, 4.38, 4.6], [17, 5.22, 5.64], [18, 5.64, 5.92], [19, 5.92, 6.22], [20, 6.22, 6.48], [21, 6.48, 6.58], [22, 6.58, 7.04], [23, 7.04, 7.7], [24, 7.7, 7.98], [25, 7.98, 8.32], [26, 8.32, 8.6], [27, 8.6, 8.96], [28, 8.96, 9.44], [29, 9.44, 9.72], [30, 9.72, 9.88], [31, 9.88, 10.12]]}, {"text": "One machine would receive the URLs to be fetched using a consistency algorithm like Paxos to decide within a group which machine will be fetching the URL.", "block": 65, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/5c8c4ceff568b52e1ebb6783579a119fbf852ba6e8ee12039d6deb077cd186e3.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.6], [2, 0.6, 0.78], [3, 0.78, 1.08], [6, 1.9, 2.02], [7, 2.02, 2.18], [8, 2.18, 2.68], [9, 2.68, 2.92], [10, 2.92, 3.08], [11, 3.08, 3.52], [12, 3.52, 4.16], [13, 4.16, 4.44], [14, 4.44, 4.96], [15, 4.96, 5.18], [16, 5.18, 5.52], [18, 5.78, 5.94], [19, 5.94, 6.2], [20, 6.2, 6.48], [21, 6.48, 6.84], [22, 6.84, 7.02], [23, 7.02, 7.14], [24, 7.14, 7.54], [25, 7.54, 7.62], [26, 7.62, 7.98]]}, {"text": "If an entire group fails, we can use the technique called “Consistent hashing” with log(M) hashing algorithms to evenly distribute the load, where M is the number of groups.", "block": 66, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/3e0a8b0b056d24521f956a545e4f7386e414ab97618691a970670e6aa5acf590.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.3], [2, 0.3, 0.6], [3, 0.6, 0.9], [4, 0.9, 1.3], [5, 1.78, 1.88], [6, 1.88, 2.06], [7, 2.06, 2.2], [8, 2.2, 2.32], [9, 2.32, 2.68], [10, 2.68, 3.16], [11, 3.16, 4.2], [12, 4.2, 4.98], [13, 4.98, 5.46], [15, 6.58, 6.86], [16, 6.86, 7.4], [17, 7.4, 7.78], [18, 7.78, 8.2], [19, 8.2, 8.62], [20, 8.62, 8.9], [21, 8.9, 9.16], [22, 9.5, 9.72], [23, 9.72, 9.94], [24, 9.94, 10.14], [25, 10.14, 10.24], [26, 10.24, 10.46], [27, 10.46, 10.66], [28, 10.66, 10.88]]}, {"text": "When a URL is found, it is hashed with k hashing functions", "block": 66, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/9b551833c6c244b23ace386d10f340ba7427a4a4b95c553169d36b080919139a.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.64], [3, 0.64, 0.86], [4, 0.86, 1.12], [5, 1.4, 1.48], [6, 1.48, 1.6], [7, 1.6, 2.0], [8, 2.0, 2.12], [10, 2.34, 2.8], [11, 2.8, 3.16]]}, {"text": "[Source]", "block": 67, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/62f7ec14de8ab9b7106637d89d7b2871cdd953f0cde2a4c762053b5326005395.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.58]]}, {"text": "Pros", "block": 68, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b629726cd0b7234801e4206158e2f3f01af19022d4ec31a955fc5ec72c680845.mp3"}, {"text": "Fully utilizes all 10,000 machines", "block": 69, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/25da3538dd189ea72f7380378c5f13e8be0ba91acd9b63b20f877dfb364918f4.mp3"}, {"text": "Minimizes network activity", "block": 70, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/3fe88e7724c29f25197f647c58d1e6bc8565b69ec11177884397838ffdea4a9f.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.58], [1, 0.58, 0.94], [2, 0.94, 1.52]]}, {"text": "Fetches each URL once :)", "block": 71, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/fdf952fc0824b45b253e4979346224fad364048e1b0467aae96d54fce50561e1.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.54], [1, 0.54, 0.78], [2, 0.78, 1.22], [3, 1.22, 1.82]]}, {"text": "Handles distributed system failures", "block": 72, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f3cd636158e5cdbeb16eb930c3db9d57226337d9a277ee89961312a828d6fe42.mp3"}, {"text": "Cons", "block": 73, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/888f900af800cdcbd6e947bed17fded4d9661d7ebf0cfc0bf47316d9b8bec67b.mp3"}, {"text": "Despite randomly assigning URLs to each group, a single group may get unlucky and be assigned either a disproportionately large number of URLs or URLs that are larger and take longer to parse.", "block": 74, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/1f8ecc792767296196075015809852b934b78be70bf29e2e6d3c4ce117bd0b07.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.4], [1, 0.4, 0.88], [2, 0.88, 1.32], [3, 1.32, 1.68], [4, 1.68, 2.08], [5, 2.08, 2.3], [6, 2.3, 2.54], [7, 2.76, 2.82], [8, 2.82, 3.06], [9, 3.06, 3.36], [13, 4.44, 4.52], [14, 4.52, 4.66], [15, 4.66, 4.98], [16, 4.98, 5.28], [17, 5.28, 5.42], [18, 5.42, 5.98], [19, 5.98, 6.5], [20, 6.5, 6.84], [21, 6.84, 7.04], [22, 7.04, 7.44], [23, 7.96, 8.14], [24, 8.14, 8.46], [25, 8.46, 8.88], [26, 8.88, 8.98], [27, 8.98, 9.38], [28, 9.38, 9.66], [29, 9.66, 9.86], [30, 9.86, 10.1], [31, 10.1, 10.32], [32, 10.32, 10.54]]}, {"text": "👉👉Have a question?", "block": 75, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/46eb735eb777b0c5e0d4bd901ea5d388223f605ab69cec1d67edf32cfa479b0d.mp3"}, {"text": "Join our FB group: System Designers", "block": 75, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/95bfbec574a5fa8015bc28445bc815ab79c82c8e73a23d6a8d3ffd7ebebd1c0c.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.3, 0.46], [2, 0.46, 0.82], [3, 0.82, 1.16], [5, 1.72, 2.28]]}, {"text": "Additional Reading", "block": 76, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/dedf11f4ebd0190c2be38fac82f713087b8861c5303b98b552f89f66229b6b73.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.48], [1, 0.48, 0.86]]}, {"text": "Decoded: Examples of How Hashing Algorithms Work (blog)", "block": 77, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/54a701084f664bbeb80994e7cf7315c606bfbc848e7394393761e631d54ee41d.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.62], [1, 0.9, 1.24], [2, 1.24, 1.52], [3, 1.52, 1.66], [4, 1.66, 2.06], [5, 2.06, 2.54], [6, 2.54, 2.96], [7, 3.16, 3.34]]}, {"text": "What is Consistent Hashing and Where is it used?", "block": 78, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/419788773fa50757be6e5376e3e5cbb07c3c7a581ac0be6fd578d509297e26d6.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.3], [2, 0.3, 0.76], [3, 0.76, 1.24], [4, 1.24, 1.6], [5, 1.6, 1.78], [6, 1.78, 1.92], [7, 1.92, 2.0], [8, 2.0, 2.3]]}, {"text": "(youtube)", "block": 78, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ad53d6a01d56904d5466bd0212109e5bdb5a5a16a9e175eac0c3ad0303b64b3c.mp3"}, {"text": "Bloom Filters (youtube)", "block": 79, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/19652d682c0ae1edeaf183cf5ee81933be0b04b66b73eced312b2e1f29951d1c.mp3"}, {"text": "Trie Data Structures (GeeksForGeeks)", "block": 80, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/c5caebd6bd386b9d042b6cbfae5368c2080c1b35f00130c20cfe83e23289aab8.mp3"}, {"text": "Scalability of Kafka Messaging using Consumer Groups (blog)", "block": 81, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/445943e1e8495bbc1b9c333585eb4e1aadc23e0152440b130ad1fe3a751d9f14.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.72], [1, 0.72, 0.88], [2, 0.88, 1.14], [3, 1.14, 1.56], [4, 1.56, 1.9], [5, 1.9, 2.4], [6, 2.4, 2.8]]}, {"text": "The Paxos Algorithm (youtube)", "block": 82, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/24706cc23c4e908589d38fefa61d56177dcc39694fa10abc24218d350fe26b81.mp3"}]}